// The chatbot capability map: ONE place that says what the assistant can do, in the words
// people use, and where the answer comes from. It is data, used by:
//   - __tests__/capabilityMap.test.js: every phrase below must resolve to the stated intent
//     and filters for every allowed role (the natural-language variation matrix);
//   - docs/chatbot-capability-map.md (generated by that test);
//   - didYouMean (the example questions offered when a message is not understood).
//
// Fields
//   id            catalog name
//   description   what it answers
//   service       the EXISTING application service / tool the answer comes from
//   roles         roles that may use it (the server re-checks on every request)
//   entities      details read from the message
//   clarifies     what is asked when a detail is missing or ambiguous
//   phrases       [{ say, intent, params? }]  params = subset that must be present
//
// Authorization is NOT decided here: it stays in permissions.js, roleScope.js and the
// services themselves.

